course: dictionary
lesson: 12923
title: Where words come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every word has a history, and that history is called its etymology. The etymology of a word tells you which language it came from and what it meant long ago. Knowing this can help you spell a word and understand what it means.
explain: Look at «bicycle». It has two parts: «bi» means two, and «cycle» means wheel. The word came into English from Greek and Latin, so its parts tell you its meaning: a vehicle with two wheels.
explain: Many English words come from other languages, such as Latin, Greek, French, Old Norse and Old English. Old Norse gave us «sky» and «egg». French gave us «beef». Words travel between languages and change over time.
fact: Etymology is the study of where words come from and how they have changed over time.
fact: The etymology of a word is its own history: the language it came from and what it meant before.
fact: «Bicycle» comes from Greek and Latin: «bi» means two, and «cycle» means wheel.
fact: Knowing a word's etymology can help you spell it and understand what it means.
fact: Folk etymology is a popular but wrong story about where a word came from.
exercise: What does etymology mean? | A type of insect with many legs | *The study of where words come from and how they have changed | A list of the hardest words in the dictionary | A word that means the same as another word
exercise: «Bicycle» has two parts, «bi» and «cycle». What does «bi» mean? | Bike | *Two | Fast | Wheel
exercise: Which two languages gave «bicycle» its parts? | Old English and French | *Greek and Latin | French and Old English | Old Norse and Latin
test: The word «sky» came into English from Old Norse. Which of these is one of the languages many English words come from? | Texting | Klingon | Emoji | *Old Norse
test: Which word means the history of a word: the language it came from and what it meant before? | Context | *Etymology | Phrase | Synonym
exam: Why is the etymology of «bicycle» useful? | It proves bicycles were invented in Scotland | It tells you the price of a bicycle | *It helps you spell and understand the word, because its parts show its meaning | It makes the word longer and harder to say
